  "I prefer modern async and await syntax for readability, but I also make sure the team understands promises deeply. I pay close attention to error handling, concurrency control, cancellation patterns, and avoiding hidden race conditions.": "i_prefer_modern_async_and_await_syntax_for_readabi_1140336925.wav",
  "How would you explain the event loop to a mid-level engineer on your team?": "how_would_you_explain_the_event_loop_to_a_midlevel_1986531272.wav",
  "I would explain that JavaScript runs tasks on a single main thread, while the event loop coordinates when queued callbacks and promise-related tasks are processed. I also use practical examples, such as timers, API calls, and UI updates, so the concept becomes easier to apply in real debugging situations.": "i_would_explain_that_javascript_runs_tasks_on_a_si_1930880749.wav",
  "Performance is important for us. What steps do you take when a JavaScript application becomes slow?": "performance_is_important_for_us_what_steps_do_you__986002625.wav",
  "First, I measure before changing anything. I profile rendering, bundle size, unnecessary network requests, memory usage, and repeated computations. Then I fix the biggest bottlenecks first and verify improvements with data.": "first_i_measure_before_changing_anything_i_profile_298038055.wav",
  "Tell me about a difficult bug you solved in a production JavaScript system.": "tell_me_about_a_difficult_bug_you_solved_in_a_prod_147021766.wav",
  "One difficult issue involved inconsistent data appearing in the interface because of overlapping requests finishing in an unexpected order. I traced the timing, reproduced the bug reliably, added safeguards to ignore stale results, and then wrote tests to prevent regression.": "one_difficult_issue_involved_inconsistent_data_app_1484651077.wav",
  "How do you ensure code quality across a JavaScript team?": "how_do_you_ensure_code_quality_across_a_javascript_1978549097.wav",
  "I focus on clear standards, strong code reviews, reliable automated tests, and shared ownership of the codebase. I also try to create an environment where engineers understand the reason behind the standards instead of following rules mechanically.": "i_focus_on_clear_standards_strong_code_reviews_rel_1954362160.wav",
